ight direction  but what you're looking at here is the  the number of operations and the  particular size of these operations and  if you look at the data carefully then  you see that all sizes are declining  rapidly except for the very largest size  so what you're seeing here is that the  number of greenhouse operations is  declining overall but we see  more of the remaining greenhouses become  larger and larger and this is a very  recent development it used to be that  the average size was around a hectare in  the netherlands and it was that for a  long time  but now in the last 10 years or so you  see you see a significant change in that  so we get fewer companies but the  companies that are remaining are larger  and then i also separated out on the  bottom here comparing the vegetable  versus the others because the vegetables  obviously are of interest to myself so  we see the same trend in the vegetable  production the number of vegetable  operations is significantly declining  over the last 10 years but the the size  of the individual operations is is  increasing and increasing quite  substantially  if you look at the overall production  area in the netherlands that has  remained the same around 10 000 hectares  but again you see some interesting  changes in the the first set of  bars you see that the vegetable  production is significantly increases  so is so is there an increase in  flowering pot plants but you see the cut  flowers  is significantly declining and hence my  comment earlier about the rose  production i think it becomes it is  becoming too expensive  to grow cut flowers in the netherlands  and and so this is this is why i think  you won't see  very many rose growers in the next 10 to  20 years anymore  if you look at the  vegetable production you see a similar  trend although here we see an increase  particularly because of tomato increase  in pepper increase  and strawberries is mentioned here also  obviously strawberry is not considered a  veg